WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.482 --> 00:00:18.825
the Queen's parade reached the croquet lawn, Alice heard a soft voice beside her.

2
00:00:19.805 --> 00:00:23.147
"It's it's a fine day," the White Rabbit said.

3
00:00:23.867 --> 00:00:25.648
He looked anxiously at Alice.

4
00:00:25.668 --> 00:00:28.810
"Very fine indeed," Alice replied.

5
00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:30.391
"Where's the Duchess?"

6
00:00:30.411 --> 00:00:32.232
"Be quiet!"

7
00:00:32.544 --> 00:00:33.785
the White Rabbit said quickly.

8
00:00:34.525 --> 00:00:37.668
He looked over his shoulder before whispering in Alice's ear.

9
00:00:37.688 --> 00:00:41.250
"The Duchess has been sentenced to death."

10
00:00:42.651 --> 00:00:44.012
Alice looked surprised.

11
00:00:44.032 --> 00:00:45.793
"What did she do?"

12
00:00:45.813 --> 00:00:51.497
"She slapped the Queen's face, and—" the White Rabbit began.

13
00:00:52.838 --> 00:00:54.599
Alice laughed nervously.

14
00:00:54.619 --> 00:00:59.662
"Oh, hush, before the Queen hears you!"

15
00:01:00.062 --> 00:01:02.304
the White Rabbit said, sounding frightened.

16
00:01:03.276 --> 00:01:09.241
"The Duchess arrived late, and—" "Go to your places!"

17
00:01:09.741 --> 00:01:10.662
the Queen roared.

18
00:01:12.123 --> 00:01:15.446
People began running in all directions, tripping over each other.

19
00:01:17.328 --> 00:01:21.171
However, they soon settled down, and the croquet game began.

20
00:01:21.191 --> 00:01:27.276
"This is the strangest croquet game I've ever seen," Alice said.

21
00:01:27.296 --> 00:01:31.640
"The balls are live hedgehogs, and the mallets are flamingos.

22
00:01:32.744 --> 00:01:35.286
And what are those soldiers doing?"

23
00:01:36.848 --> 00:01:40.271
The soldiers were bending over so their hands touched the ground.

24
00:01:40.291 --> 00:01:42.333
"Oh, I see!

25
00:01:42.353 --> 00:01:43.614
They're the wickets!"

26
00:01:44.074 --> 00:01:44.935
Alice exclaimed.

27
00:01:49.599 --> 00:01:51.201
She picked up her flamingo.

28
00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:54.143
But her flamingo wouldn't cooperate.

29
00:01:55.805 --> 00:01:59.148
Alice couldn't figure out how to hold it as a mallet.

30
00:02:00.468 --> 00:02:05.571
The bird kept looking at her with a puzzled expression, which only made Alice laugh.

31
00:02:07.192 --> 00:02:11.714
As for her hedgehog, it unrolled itself and began to walk away.

32
00:02:16.397 --> 00:02:18.778
The soldiers kept getting up to stretch.

33
00:02:19.899 --> 00:02:22.400
And the ground was too rough to play on.

34
00:02:26.042 --> 00:02:28.764
is a hard way to play croquet," Alice said.

35
00:02:30.368 --> 00:02:31.988
The players didn't take turns.

36
00:02:32.609 --> 00:02:37.230
Instead they all made their shots at once, which led to many arguments.

37
00:02:39.731 --> 00:02:43.952
Soon the Queen was stomping around, shouting, "Off with his head!

38
00:02:44.372 --> 00:02:45.552
Off with her head!"

39
00:02:46.592 --> 00:02:48.713
Alice began to feel uneasy.

40
00:02:48.733 --> 00:02:53.034
"I hope I don't do anything to upset the Queen," she thought.

41
00:02:53.054 --> 00:02:54.935
"That could be dangerous."

42
00:02:56.335 --> 00:03:01.089
Suddenly she saw something odd floating in the air—a grin.

43
00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:04.051
The image grew clearer.

44
00:03:04.071 --> 00:03:06.672
"It's the Cheshire Cat!"

45
00:03:07.073 --> 00:03:08.073
Alice said happily.

46
00:03:08.093 --> 00:03:10.475
"Now I'll have somebody to talk to."

47
00:03:10.495 --> 00:03:14.598
"How are you doing?"

48
00:03:15.118 --> 00:03:16.419
the Cheshire Cat asked.

49
00:03:16.439 --> 00:03:23.064
"There's no use replying until his ears show up," Alice said to herself.

50
00:03:24.004 --> 00:03:24.985
"He can't hear me yet."

51
00:03:25.986 --> 00:03:29.128
In another minute the Cheshire Cat's whole head was visible.

52
00:03:30.436 --> 00:03:34.278
Alice put down her flamingo and began to describe the croquet game.

53
00:03:35.338 --> 00:03:38.600
Meanwhile the Cheshire Cat's body remained invisible.

54
00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:42.962
"Nobody plays fairly," Alice complained.

55
00:03:42.982 --> 00:03:47.464
"And it's so difficult using live animals and soldiers."

56
00:03:52.146 --> 00:03:54.427
do you like the Queen?"

57
00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:56.788
the Cheshire Cat asked quietly.

58
00:03:58.204 --> 00:04:00.165
"I don't like her at all," Alice said.

59
00:04:00.185 --> 00:04:06.568
"She's so—" Just then Alice noticed the Queen listening nearby.

60
00:04:07.568 --> 00:04:08.208
She blushed.

61
00:04:08.228 --> 00:04:14.611
"I mean, the Queen is likely to win, so it's not worth finishing the game."

62
00:04:15.892 --> 00:04:17.953
The Queen smiled and passed by.

63
00:04:20.434 --> 00:04:25.236
As Alice continued to talk, the King approached and stared at the Cheshire Cat's head.

64
00:04:29.132 --> 00:04:31.434
"Who are you talking to?"

65
00:04:31.995 --> 00:04:33.196
the King asked Alice.

66
00:04:33.216 --> 00:04:37.840
"This is a good friend of mine, the Cheshire Cat," she said.

67
00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:39.601
"Let me introduce you."

68
00:04:39.621 --> 00:04:43.805
"I don't like the look of that cat at all.

69
00:04:44.806 --> 00:04:47.668
He must be removed at once."

70
00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:51.251
The King called out to the Queen.

71
00:04:51.271 --> 00:04:53.013
"My dear!

72
00:04:53.553 --> 00:04:56.316
Please have this cat removed!"

73
00:04:57.344 --> 00:05:01.751
The Queen had only one way of dealing with problems, large or small.

74
00:05:01.771 --> 00:05:03.974
"Off with his head!"

75
00:05:04.515 --> 00:05:05.076
she cried.

76
00:05:06.098 --> 00:05:08.582
The King went to fetch the Executioner.
